WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.610
- Are you interested to
get into a high profile

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.730
career like consulting or banking?

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.260
Because if you do, your
application for sure

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.430
needs to contain two documents.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.830
First, your cover letter,
and second your CV.

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:13.300
So I already made some videos

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.430
talking about what it
takes to write a great CV.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.730
And I even made one video
showing you the very CV

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:23.300
that I used to successfully
apply to McKinsey

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.330
as a consultant.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.270
If you haven't seen it yet

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.130
and wanna check it out, no problem,

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.590
there's a link somewhere above
here where I will insert it.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.240
As I got lots of positive feedback

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.500
on the video I now want to
follow it up with a second video,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.050
showing you how the actual
cover letter looked like

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:40.370
that I used to successfully
apply to McKinsey in Germany.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.490
In this video, I will walk
through paragraph by paragraph

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:45.380
through the cover letter that I used

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.050
for my McKinsey application.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:48.630
And given that this application

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.270
was already a couple of years ago,

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.170
I will also share some reflections.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.290
What I would probably change today

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:56.320
if I would now need to
write such a cover letter

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.960
because I by no means believe

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.790
that my old cover letter was perfect.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.450
Though of course it was good enough

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.070
to get invited to the interview,

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:05.110
and then later also to
get me into the firm.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:07.740
So welcome to another coffee
break here on my channel

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.850
Firm Learning, my name is Heinrich,

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:12.790
and on my channel I want to
help you to become successful

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:14.610
in the first years of your career.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:16.277
Now, before we jump into the cover letter,

00:01:16.277 --> 00:01:19.910
now for the sake of transparency,
I did a couple of changes.

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:23.330
So first I translated the
whole cover letter in English

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.080
because I applied in German.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.100
And then also took out
some personal information

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.800
just to protect my privacy
and I also changed some

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.300
minor details also just to protect myself.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.490
But overall these changes are rather minor

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.410
so you can treat it as the
actual cover letter that I used.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.000
But now let's jump into it.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.750
So I have the cover
letter here in front of me

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.590
and indeed now let's go over
it paragraph by paragraph.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:44.423
And first of all,

00:01:44.423 --> 00:01:46.070
make sure that you start your cover letter

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:48.440
with a formal letterhead that is formative

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:51.030
just in the way that is
customary for your region.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.930
So usually this will
look something like this.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:56.090
So you start with your own
name, with your address

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:57.160
in the top right.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.900
Then later the recruiter name,

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:00.230
then the company name,

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.220
and then the office
address of the company.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:05.010
Here it's always great to
include the actual name

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.690
of the recruiter that will
then read your application.

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:09.710
Usually if you Google
the head of recruiting

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.847
or something like that, this
will be possible for you.

00:02:11.847 --> 00:02:14.160
And this makes it always
a bit more personal

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.780
than just writing the company name.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.540
And it shows that you did a
minimal amount of research

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.730
just here in the beginning.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:22.780
Then it is customary to include
the location and the date

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.200
here in the right-hand
side of the cover letter.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.380
And then it's good practice
to include a subject line

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.830
at the beginning of your
cover letter in bold,

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.950
just to make it clear what
this letter is all about.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.850
So here I wrote application
for a consulting internship

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.530
position at McKinsey &amp; Company.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:41.500
Because when I applied to
McKinsey, I applied as an intern.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.060
And then after the internship
I got a full-time offer.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:45.320
So this is how I got in.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.210
So then clearly state the objective

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:49.490
of your letter here in
such a subject line.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:51.730
Next you formally address your recruiter.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.740
And then you start with
the first paragraph

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.290
of the actual application.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.210
Now probably one of the
things that I've seen

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.950
most people do wrong,

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.217
if people send me cover letters

00:03:00.217 --> 00:03:01.880
and just ask me to review them.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.630
And this will be what you write
in the very first paragraph.

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:07.180
In the spirit of top-down communication,

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.610
and if you do not know what
top-down communication is

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:10.740
I made a video about that.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.520
I will link at somewhere above here.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.010
But in the spirit of
top-down communication,

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:18.350
do yourself a favor and in
the very first paragraph,

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.050
very precisely state what you want.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.830
And in the case of an application,

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.470
I would strongly recommend
you to always include

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.530
three key pieces of information.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:30.060
So the first is what is the position

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.180
that you are applying to.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:32.540
So in my case, this was here

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.320
the business analyst intern position.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.480
The second information should
be what is the office location

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.410
that you are applying to?

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.390
What office would you
be interested to join?

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:43.250
And then third, clearly
state your availability.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:45.260
So when do you wanna do the internship?

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:47.730
When do you wanna start
for full-time position?

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.180
And if it is for an internship,

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:52.470
indeed also clearly state
what the time duration

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:53.560
is that you wanna do.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:56.170
And of course here make sure
to check the requirements

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.300
of your firms because many
firms have a minimum duration,

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.170
or sometimes also maximum duration

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.870
that an internship can take.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.250
So make sure that you
meet these requirements

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.080
when you phrase it here
in the first paragraph.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.070
So these are key information
to take in for any recruiter.

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:11.880
So don't hide information like this

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.510
somewhere in the middle of your body,

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.290
but make sure to include this
in the very first paragraph.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.810
Next, provide some context
where you currently stand

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:20.820
in your life, so in your
educational journey,

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.060
on your career journey.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.680
So if you are a student, right,

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.870
what you're currently studying,

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.120
and also when do you expect to graduate.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.450
Because this of course will
be relevant information.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:30.700
When you are an experienced hire,

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.020
so here clearly state whether

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.630
you are currently employed or not.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:36.140
And if you are employed,
when you could quit the job,

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.710
when you could quit the company.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.097
So just make it really
clear for the recruiter

00:04:39.097 --> 00:04:42.100
where you currently
stand in your educational

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.260
or professional journey,

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:45.130
to have them put you into the right box.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.420
So here I wrote about that
I was currently at the time

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.270
studying at the University of Munich.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.080
I told them when I expected to graduate,

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.100
I told them what I was currently studying

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.140
and also tried here to make
a link to how my studies

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:58.300
relate now to the requirements of the job.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:59.940
Now let's move to the third paragraph.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.190
And here in the third paragraph,

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:04.230
I would recommend you to
now pull out one or two key

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:06.120
instances of experience,

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.270
key things that you did in your life

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:11.240
that you believe are
really the cherry on top

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.140
of your application.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:15.150
What are really the things
that you stand out for?

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.810
What is your spike?

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:18.580
What is the spike in your application?

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.930
No, of course this will
often also be included

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.060
in your cover letter,

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.940
but really try to find something

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.930
that now the recruiter can
take and use as an information,

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.860
if they want to defend your case,

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.650
what is really the punchline,

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.610
why they should invite
you to an interview.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:35.040
So here now I talked about
a special study program

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.420
that I attended in Munich.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:38.850
It is quite a renowned
program in Munich at least.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.510
And then I also told them how this really

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:41.570
relates to the job.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:44.670
So talking about these project
based activities that I did,

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.930
and also linking it to an
internship at Accenture,

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.970
at another consulting
firm that I did earlier.

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:51.410
And here the important phrase to remember,

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:55.970
that you should really have in
your mind is show don't tell.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:57.610
So what many people do wrong

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.700
is they tell in their cover letter,

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:01.840
they tell in their CV, instead of showing.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.940
So what this means is
they will write things

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:07.160
like I am smart, I am a great team player,

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:09.710
I am creative, I think out of the box.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:12.920
So people pretty much
just make bold claims

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:14.060
about themselves.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:17.410
But the problem with this is
of course that talk is cheap.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.380
Everybody can just write
things like that into their CV

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.420
or into their cover letter.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:24.900
No way this really distinguishes
you from other candidates.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:28.110
So instead of making cheap
claims about yourself,

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.850
rather show what you're capable of doing,

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:34.960
mention the specific things
that you did that really portray

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.640
these virtues that you
can bring to the table.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.210
So instead of just talking
about how you would be great in

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.730
project based environments,

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:44.360
just rather show the actual
experiences that you already

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.680
collected, where you worked in projects,

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:48.130
where you delivered impact,

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.730
where you showed that you can bring

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:51.230
all these virtues to the table.

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:53.280
And now looking critically
at my cover letter

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.260
I think that this paragraph
is not strong enough.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.210
So if you read this,

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:59.610
while this might be great
and some nice achievements,

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:02.410
this is now not something that
leaves you in complete awe,

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:05.280
this just doesn't sound
like a super awesome

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.530
and great achievement.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.570
So that time, if I would rewrite it today,

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:12.250
I would dig even deeper
into what the real spikes

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:14.610
in my profile are that I really wanna show

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:15.540
here to the recruiters.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.710
So now just to do a very short break here,

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:19.820
because if you find this to be helpful,

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.880
I now have a new offering for you.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:25.010
Because I put together
a cover letter template

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.130
that is very similar to this cover letter.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.410
So you get a cover letter
very similar to this

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:31.910
in an open Microsoft Word format

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.830
with a couple of additional remarks

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:35.570
that will help you to
write your cover letter.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:37.450
So this would help you as a starting point

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:39.280
to put your own cover letter together,

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:41.530
check out the link in
the video description

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:43.160
to my cover letter template.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.830
I hope this will be of value to you,

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.210
but now back to my cover letter.

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:48.290
So what I did here in my fourth paragraph

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:50.550
is that I talked about another key quality

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:53.280
that I believe that I would
be able to bring to the table

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:54.840
based on my past experience.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:57.130
So pretty much a mirror
of the third paragraph,

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:59.590
but bringing in another
point, another spike

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:01.330
that I believe would have really helped me

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.163
in the application.

00:08:02.163 --> 00:08:05.290
So specifically I wanted to
stress some experiences of mine

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.850
in the client service,

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.940
just to show that I would be able to face

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:12.040
and handle difficult client
situations on the job.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.510
Again now, when I read this today,

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.690
probably I would have
written something else

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:17.210
in this fourth paragraph,

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:20.060
and this is rather to make
it more about motivation.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:23.300
So, but this is okay if you
have really something strong

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:24.260
that you want to share,

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:26.610
probably it's a good
idea to talk a little bit

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.980
also about what actually motivates you

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.330
to become a consultant.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:32.040
Why do you wanna do this job?

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:35.700
And then also why you
chose this specific firm

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.010
over other firms, right?

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:40.660
So for instance, if you apply
to BCG, or Bain, or McKinsey,

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:44.220
what is your motivation to
specifically apply to that firm

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:45.410
over some other firms.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:47.510
And here now if you believe
that you have no clue

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:49.650
why you wanna pick that specific firm,

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:52.810
I would recommend you to talk
to some alums of these firms.

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:55.250
They will easily be able to
tell you some very specific

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.520
things that make this firm very special,

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.240
and then this is indeed
what you can write.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.540
But here also the truth
is that the recruiters

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:04.030
are very much aware of the
companies like McKinsey,

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.110
BCG, or Bain.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:07.460
To some extent they are pretty similar

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:10.180
so the expectation is not
that now you will come up

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:12.360
with some crazy points here right.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.790
But of course, it's
always just nice to show

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:17.330
that you have some real
passion for a company.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:18.920
People just love to read that,

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.780
why their own firm is special.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.390
So just dig deep here a bit,

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:25.120
just to come up with some
nice and thoughtful points.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:26.410
Now in the last paragraph,

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:28.890
I will talk about what
the next step would be

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:30.110
from your perspective.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:31.790
So what would you like them to do now?

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:32.757
What is your ask now?

00:09:32.757 --> 00:09:34.950
And of course in a recruiting context,

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.440
usually next step is then to
be invited to an interview.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:38.910
So yeah, I would write exactly that,

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:41.020
write that you will be
glad for an opportunity

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:43.090
to introduce yourself in an interview.

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:45.730
And then the recruiter can
use this to make a reference

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.010
to that when they contact you.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:49.570
So let me now share three key reflections

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:51.330
and recommendations that I can give you

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:52.610
regarding your cover letter.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:55.160
First, you need to realize
that the cover letter

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.440
is a hygiene factor.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:59.610
Pretty much nobody gets invited
because their cover letter

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:01.560
is so awesome, so don't
freak out about it.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:03.930
Follow this basic clean, simple structure,

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:04.880
and you will be fine.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:07.770
Use it as a means to convey
the key pieces of information

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:09.360
that you wanna let the recruiter know.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.740
And then also use it to really underline

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.980
the key strength of your profile.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:16.480
Use the cover letter to
really help the recruiter

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:17.893
understand what the strongest aspects

00:10:17.893 --> 00:10:19.390
of your application are.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:22.670
Second, don't make the
mistake of just repeating

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:23.810
what is on your CV.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.250
People will have your CV,

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.290
they will look very diligently at your CV.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:28.690
So don't just in a sterile way

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.580
copy what you wrote in the CV,

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:33.520
but rather use the cover
letter to add some color,

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.690
to add some additional
pieces of information

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.040
that you will usually not find on your CV

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.560
and therefore to really add
value with your cover letter.

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.630
Throughout the layout, and here make sure

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:45.650
that your cover letter is
no longer than one page.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:48.700
Nobody wants to read a
two page cover letter.

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:50.090
Keep it brief and simple,

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:52.040
and the recruiter will
be thankful for that.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:55.330
And then also avoid crazy
formatting on your cover letter.

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:57.360
Your cover letter just
needs to be black and white.

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:00.140
A very simple, basic font like Arial.

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:02.390
Do not use any crazy formatting,

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:04.370
any crazy colors, anything like that.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:06.690
This will for sure not help
you in your application,

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:09.010
keep it strictly professional
and you will be fine.

